KN-H2 UserPromptSubmit probe results (muse-bin-1.4.14-R7309.1)
============================================================
Method: temporary user-level UserPromptSubmit hook, one `muse exec` per
variant asking "What is the secret word? Reply with one word.", settings
restored byte-identical after every run. Hook fired on all runs (stdin
captured each time).

1b: nested hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext WITHOUT trailing newline
  stdout: {"hookSpecificOutput":{"hookEventName":"UserPromptSubmit",
            "additionalContext":"The secret word is PINEAPPLE."}}  (no \n)
  reply: Unavailable  -> context NOT delivered

1c-a: nested shape WITH trailing newline
  reply: PINEAPPLE  -> DELIVERED
  hook_run_terminal: status=completed exit=0 error=null effects=["context"]

1c-b: top-level {"additionalContext": ...} + newline
  reply: Unknown  -> NOT delivered
  hook_run_terminal: status=failed exit=0
    error="unsupported `additionalContext` in output of UserPromptSubmit
            hook output", stdout echoed back unconsumed, no effects

1c-c: plain text stdout "The secret word is PINEAPPLE." + newline
  reply: PINEAPPLE  -> DELIVERED
  hook_run_terminal: status=completed exit=0 error=null effects=["context"]

1c-d: top-level {"systemMessage": ...} + newline
  reply: unknown  -> NOT model-visible
  hook_run_terminal: status=completed exit=0 error=null,
    system_message recorded on the record, no effects (display channel)

Captured UserPromptSubmit stdin keys (verbatim, step 1):
  hook_event_name, prompt, session_id, turn_id, cwd, transcript_path,
  model, permission_mode, model_provider

Rules for knack/hooks/warn.py (proven, do not re-prove):
- Nested envelope + trailing \n is the only JSON shape that injects.
- print() (which appends \n) is REQUIRED; printf-without-newline fails
  silently (exit 0, model never sees the context).
- Top-level additionalContext is rejected; the rejection is silent at the
  CLI and visible only in `muse export`.
- Never emit a "decision" key: decision:block cancels the turn, and warn
  must never block.
